He told me that sn[printf has] a[ bit of] useful behaviour: if you pass it a NULL pointer and 0 as the first two arguments, it will return the[ number] of bytes that would be needed if we wanted to hold the full string. Without the 0 byte at the end, because C[ was] made to inf[uriate] you1.
Fig. 2: Figure 1, fixed.
